{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_1647729865#0_3617397938","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to vicarious trauma and explicitly promises definition, symptoms, and how to cope with it.","learned":"Vicarious trauma is described as trauma from indirect exposure to traumatic events, especially among helpers; the page includes symptoms and coping strategies."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1006","reason":"The current focused query is producing highly relevant, dedicated resources, so continue retrieving more results from it."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1006"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_1647729865#1_3617399591","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1006","rank":2,"snippet":"Cope with it Vicarious Trauma: When Empathy Goes Too Far & How to Cope with it What is Vicarious Trauma & Who is Susceptible to it? Signs and Symptoms of Vicarious Trauma How to Treat Vicarious Trauma Methods To Treat Vicarious Trauma Trauma-Focused Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (TF-CBT): Eye Movement Desensitization and Reprocessing (EMDR): Get Professional Help \" , \"segment\": \"Often, people who help behind the scenes in helping those with trauma might neglect their own exposure. In this article, you will learn what Vicarious Trauma is, some of the <cover>symptoms associated with it. You will also learn how to cope with Vicarious Trauma </cover>so that you can live a happy and balanced professional life. What is Vicarious Trauma & Who is Susceptible to it? Vicarious Trauma refers to the trauma you may experience when being indirectly exposed to a traumatic event. It could be a situation where the life of another person was being threatened or witnessing the death of someone else. It is as if you’ve taken this trauma as your own, and it has triggered a shocking reaction in your emotions and actions. Vicarious Trauma typically involves a change in personal beliefs about the "}}
