{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1687373808#10_2612771544","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from the dedicated GoodTherapy vicarious trauma page, with headings on understanding, symptoms, mental health, and self-care practices; the visible passage cites foundational work on treating vicarious traumatization/secondary traumatic stress, though it is duplicate evidence from the same source.","learned":"The term vicarious traumatization is associated with secondary traumatic stress and compassion fatigue literature, including treatment/coping resources for those who treat traumatized people."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1007","reason":"The alternate-term query may surface additional dedicated resources on vicarious traumatization and coping; continue past this duplicate result."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1007"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2628985626#11_3662379229","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1007","rank":2,"snippet":"cases, forensic nurses must be able to preemptively address mental health issues as well. Jarvis notes that forensic nurses often work autonomously and must use critical thinking to decide on the next best steps in an exam. A strong sense of self: Many helpers who work with those affected by trauma often experience a sort of secondhand trauma themselves, also called <cover>vicarious traumatization. Characterized by a lack of personal meaning and hope, it can affect the trauma helper’s marriage, mental health, children and friendships. Having a support system, a strong belief system and effective and healthy coping strategies can help forensic nurses immensely in maintaining their ability to have empathy daily for their patients and continue to be an advocate for them. Individualization: Each person reacts differently to trauma and a forensic nurse has to be sensitive to each patient’s state. Schmitz loves this aspect of the job.\" , \"start_char\": 6449.000000 , \"title\": \"What Is </cover>Forensic Nursing? Investigating the Crossover of Law and Medicine | Rasmussen University\" , \"url\": \"https://www.rasmussen.edu/degrees/nursing/blog/what-is-forensic-nursing/\" }"}}
