{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1688725936#0_2614437562","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage is closely related and gives signs of vicarious/secondary trauma and the importance of self-care, but the document appears primarily framed around compassion fatigue for helping professionals rather than being dedicated specifically to answering what vicarious trauma is and how to cope with it.","learned":"Helpers can experience vicarious trauma through clients' stories; warning signs include preoccupation with traumatic stories, emotional distress, stress-related physical symptoms, burnout, hopelessness, irritability, and self-isolation, and self-care is emphasized."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"vicarious trauma\" toolkit (+ definition \"what is\") (+ coping \"self care\" strategies))","reason":"A toolkit-oriented query should find dedicated organizational resources that define vicarious trauma and provide coping/self-care strategies."}}
