{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_168597421#6_340984647","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from the dedicated Edutopia article on vicarious trauma in teachers, directly describing symptoms and offering coping strategies such as talking with a therapist, partner, or colleagues; it is relevant but duplicates the same source as an earlier result.","learned":"For teachers coping with vicarious/secondary trauma, talking it out with a therapist, partner, or colleagues can help process the trauma and related emotions."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1011","reason":"Continue the productive coping-strategies query a little further to look for additional distinct dedicated sources beyond the repeated Edutopia and Wikipedia results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1011"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_168597421#4_340980748","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1011","rank":6,"snippet":"\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_168597421#4_340980748\" , \"end_char\": 3882.000000 , \"headings\": \"When Students Are Traumatized, Teachers Are Too Teacher Wellness When Students Are Traumatized, Teachers Are Too By Emelina Minero The Real Costs of Trauma Talking it Out Building <cover>Coping Strategies Establishing Coming Home Rituals \" , \"segment\": \"In schools, the signs of trauma may be seen in a student acting out in class, or they could be more subtle—like failure to make eye contact or repeatedly tapping a foot. ( To learn more about how trauma impacts students, read “ Brains in Pain Cannot Learn! ”) For teachers, who are directly exposed to a large number of young people with trauma in their work, a secondary type of trauma, known as vicarious trauma, </cover>is a big risk. Sometimes called the “cost of caring,” vicarious trauma can result from “hearing [people’s] trauma stories and becom [ing] witnesses to the pain, fear, and terror that trauma survivors have endured,” according to the American Counseling Association. “Being a teacher is a stressful enough job, but teachers are now responsible for a lot "}}
