{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"warning signs\" \"vicarious trauma\" (+ coping strategies \"self-care\" prevention) (+ definition symptoms))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_158990471#13_315235734","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1021","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_158990471#13_315235734\" , \"end_char\": 8150.000000 , \"headings\": \"Understand & Overcome Your Compassion Fatigue: An Online Guide Understand & Overcome Your Compassion Fatigue: An Online Guide Compassion Fatigue Basics The Process: Steps to Fatigue Clearing Up Terminology Compassion fatigue is synonymous with secondary traumatic stress: Compassion fatigue is not burnout: Compassion satisfaction is the opposite of compassion fatigue: Some symptoms of compassion fatigue mimic PTSD:<cover>Vicarious Trauma shares similar symptoms with compassion fatigue: Self-Assessment Questionnaire: Are You Vulnerable? Additional Warning Signs and Symptoms Developing a Self-Care </cover>Plan to Manage Your Compassion Fatigue How to Avoid Compassion Fatigue: Preventative Care 1. Know that putting yourself first isn’t selfish 2. Create emotional boundaries 3. Find your support network (Interview) A Nurse’s Experience with Compassion Fatigue 1. How/when did you first learn about secondary traumatic stress and compassion fatigue? 2. When did you know you were dealing with symptoms? 3. What are some steps you took to address compassion fatigue? 4. How long did it take to come out of that season? 5. How do you stay ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_158990471#10_315227890","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_158990471#9_315225168","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
