{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1688725936#5_2614446007","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated article on vicarious trauma and self-care for therapists, directly listing coping/self-care practices such as relaxation, nature, nonwork activities, creative pursuits, and meeting with a therapist to build coping skills and reduce risk.","learned":"Coping strategies can include relaxation, spending time in nature, activities outside work, creative hobbies, professional counseling, and a self-care plan."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1022","reason":"The query is returning dedicated vicarious-trauma self-care resources for helping professionals, so continue to seek additional grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1022"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_664821645#2_1259363627","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1022","rank":4,"snippet":"\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_664821645#2_1259363627\" , \"end_char\": 3079.000000 , \"headings\": \"10 Self-Care Tips for Psychologists, Therapists, and Counselors 10 Self-Care Tips for Psychologists, Therapists, and <cover>Counselors This Article Contains: Mental Health and the Therapist Macro and Micro Self-Care Macro self-care Health care Taking a vacation Balance Treats Micro self-care 8 Strategies for Coping With Work Stress 1. Feeling love 2. Circle of care 3. Tea in a bubble 4. 4–7–8 Breath 5. Daily intention 6. Embrace yourself 7. Five senses 8. Reflection on impermanence PositivePsychology.com’s Resources A Take-Home Message References How useful was this article to you? About the Author Categories Legal Company Details Contact \" , \"segment\": \"Without adequate care, the mental health professional is equally at risk of “burnout, vicarious trauma, </cover>and compassion fatigue,” says Ashley Davis Bush (2015). And while the warning is stark, it is of genuine concern for anyone whose focus is others’ wellbeing. A report from 1990 found that nurses, therapists, social workers, and psychologists in psychiatric hospitals faced high occupational burnout "}}
