{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_664821645#2_1259363627","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is a general self-care article for psychologists, therapists, and counselors rather than being dedicated to vicarious trauma, but it explicitly identifies vicarious trauma as a risk for mental health professionals and provides work-stress/self-care strategies that are adjacent coping evidence.","learned":"Mental health professionals are at risk of burnout, vicarious trauma, and compassion fatigue without adequate self-care; general coping strategies may include vacations, balance, breathing exercises, reflection, and social support."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"vicarious trauma\" \"coping strategies\" \"self-care\" (+ therapists counselors \"helping professionals\"))","reason":"Refine toward pages explicitly centered on vicarious trauma coping strategies and self-care for helping professionals, where grade-3 dedicated evidence is more likely than general self-care pages."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"vicarious trauma\" \"coping strategies\" \"self-care\" (+ therapists counselors \"helping professionals\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689932687#6_2616445571","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1023","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689932687#6_2616445571\" , \"end_char\": 5645.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Cost of Caring: 10 Ways to Prevent Compassion Fatigue The Cost of Caring: 10 Ways to Prevent Compassion Fatigue 1. Get Educated 2. Practice <cover>Self-Care 3. Set Emotional Boundaries 4. Engage in Outside Hobbies 5. Cultivate Healthy Friendships Outside of Work 6. Keep a Journal 7. Boost Your Resiliency 8. Use Positive Coping Strategies 9. Identify Workplace Strategies 10. Seek Personal Therapy References: Last Update: 03-26-2020 \" , \"segment\": \"vicarious trauma,” Urdang said. “ Taking the very best care of yourself includes setting limits.” 3. Set Emotional Boundaries It can be especially important for therapists, </cover>social workers, nurses, and caregivers alike to set firm emotional boundaries to protect themselves. Empathy and compassion are generally at the forefront of a human services career. The challenge is to remain compassionate, empathetic, and supportive of others without becoming overly involved and taking on another’s pain. Setting emotional boundaries helps maintain a connection while still remembering and honoring the fact that you are a separate "}}
