{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"secondhand trauma\" \"vicarious trauma\" (+ cope coping \"self-care\" strategies) (+ signs symptoms definition))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_158990471#2_315204961","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1031","rank":1,"snippet":"satisfaction is the opposite of compassion fatigue: Some symptoms of compassion fatigue mimic PTSD:<cover>Vicarious Trauma shares similar symptoms with compassion fatigue: Self-Assessment Questionnaire: Are You Vulnerable? Additional Warning Signs and Symptoms Developing a Self-Care Plan to Manage Your Compassion Fatigue How to Avoid Compassion Fatigue: Preventative Care 1. Know that putting yourself first isn’t selfish 2. Create emotional boundaries 3. Find your support network (Interview) A Nurse’s Experience with Compassion Fatigue 1. How/when did you first learn about secondary traumatic stress and compassion fatigue? 2. When did you know you were dealing with symptoms? 3. What are some steps you took to address compassion fatigue? 4. How long did it take to come out of that season? 5. How do you stay proactive to guard against compassion fatigue? 6. Are there particular resources you’ve sought out? 7. What advice would you give to healthcare professionals in a similar situation? Resources to Take Action Against Compassion Fatigue \" , \"segment\": \"The rewards that come from this line of work are immense, but experiencing secondhand trauma </cover>can take its toll, as well. Compassion fatigue refers to the emotional, physical, cognitive, and "}}
